# CP2K twin (offline oracle) — collinear UKS Berry-phase dipole, bulk Si (GPW)
# Pairs with regressions/gpw/periodic-berry-gpw-uks/REFERENCE.md.
# Never executed at ctest/regression time (offline pin only).
#
# Matched algorithm twin of ATV cpu::gpw::BerryPolarization on collinear UKS
# (n_alpha = n_beta, dual-channel KSV string phases). CP2K evaluates the same
# observable via &MOMENTS PERIODIC T (Berry-phase / Resta operator) on
# Quickstep GPW with LSD / MULTIPLICITY 1: GTH + Gaussian MOLOPT, PADE,
# orthorhombic BCT diamond Si.
#
# NOTE: qs_moment_kpoints (PERIODIC moments under &KPOINTS) is closed-shell
# only in CP2K 2026.1 (CPASSERT SIZE(matrix_ks_kp,1)==1 in qs_moments.F). The
# collinear UKS Berry path is therefore pinned at Γ via qs_moment_berry_phase,
# which loops over nspins. Same algorithm class (modern theory of
# polarization / Berry phase); k-mesh is a twin discretization choice, not a
# different method family. Absolute phases may differ by a quantum; symmetry
# pins (half-quantum lattice, ASR Z*=0) are the scientific content of the reg.
#
# Wall twin: time this single ENERGY job (1 MPI × fixed OMP) vs one ATV
# string-mesh SCF+Berry direction (not multi-gate reg wall).

&GLOBAL
  PROJECT si_periodic_berry_gpw_uks
  RUN_TYPE ENERGY
  PRINT_LEVEL MEDIUM
&END GLOBAL
&FORCE_EVAL
  METHOD Quickstep
  &DFT
    BASIS_SET_FILE_NAME BASIS_MOLOPT
    POTENTIAL_FILE_NAME GTH_POTENTIALS
    LSD
    MULTIPLICITY 1
    &QS
      EPS_DEFAULT 1.0E-10
    &END QS
    &MGRID
      CUTOFF 80
      REL_CUTOFF 40
    &END MGRID
    &SCF
      SCF_GUESS ATOMIC
      EPS_SCF 1.0E-7
      MAX_SCF 60
    &END SCF
    &XC
      &XC_FUNCTIONAL PADE
      &END XC_FUNCTIONAL
    &END XC
    &PRINT
      &MOMENTS
        PERIODIC T
        REFERENCE COM
      &END MOMENTS
    &END PRINT
  &END DFT
  &SUBSYS
    &CELL
      # BCT diamond Si orthorhombic: a/√2, a/√2, a with a = 5.43 Å
      ABC 3.83959 3.83959 5.43
      PERIODIC XYZ
    &END CELL
    &COORD
      Si  0.00000  0.00000  0.00000
      Si  1.91980  1.91980  2.71500
      Si  1.91980  0.00000  1.35750
      Si  0.00000  1.91980  4.07250
      # displaced twin: move atom 2 by +0.02 * C = (0, 0, 0.1086)
    &END COORD
    &KIND Si
      BASIS_SET DZVP-MOLOPT-GTH
      POTENTIAL GTH-PADE-q4
    &END KIND
  &END SUBSYS
&END FORCE_EVAL
